Copyright 2026 fastmathverify contributors. Licensed under the Apache License 2.0.

This project reimplements the behaviour of:

  Math-Verify (https://github.com/huggingface/Math-Verify)
  Copyright The HuggingFace Team. Apache License 2.0.
  The answer-extraction regular expressions and comparison rules are ported from it.

  latex2sympy2_extended (https://github.com/huggingface/latex2sympy2_extended)
  Copyright 2016 latex2sympy and The HuggingFace Team. MIT License
  (see grammar/LICENSE-latex2sympy2_extended.txt).
  grammar/PS.g4 and the parser generated from it (src/gen/) derive from its grammar;
  src/normalize.rs and src/convert.rs port its normalization and conversion logic.

Vendored dependency:

  antlr4rust 0.6.0 (https://github.com/antlr4rust/antlr4), BSD 3-Clause License
  (vendor/antlr4rust/LICENSE.txt). Modified: `prediction_mode` is made public in
  vendor/antlr4rust/src/lib.rs so the parser can use SLL prediction.

tests/data/regression.jsonl contains short excerpts (answers and solutions) from:
- OpenR1-Math-220k (https://huggingface.co/datasets/open-r1/OpenR1-Math-220k), Apache-2.0
- DeepScaleR-Preview-Dataset (https://huggingface.co/datasets/agentica-org/DeepScaleR-Preview-Dataset), MIT
- MATH-500 (https://huggingface.co/datasets/HuggingFaceH4/MATH-500), a subset of the MATH
  dataset by Hendrycks et al. (MIT)
